The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Missing call to MCS FLR handler
// rvu_detach_rsrcs(rvu, NULL, pcifunc);
```
Reason:
The absence of a call to the MCS FLR handler when MCS resources are attached to a PF/VF during a Function Level Reset (FLR) means that the necessary cleanup of MCS resources is not performed, which can lead to resource leaks or undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (rvu->mcs_blk_cnt)
    rvu_mcs_flr_handler(rvu, pcifunc);
```
Reason:
This addition ensures that the MCS FLR handler is called when MCS resources are present, allowing for the proper cleanup of these resources during the FLR process, thus preventing potential resource leaks or undefined behavior.

